Hey you,

I know you’re trying really hard to be good. To be liked. To not disappoint anyone. You think if you just work a little harder, stay a little quieter, get a little better, everything will finally feel safe.

But here’s something no one told you:

You don’t have to earn love. You don’t have to earn rest. You don’t have to earn being enough.

The things you’re insecure about? They won’t define you. The moments you replay at night, embarrassed and wishing you were different? They’ll fade. And one day, you’ll realize most people were too busy worrying about themselves to notice the things you’re still ashamed of.

You’re not “too sensitive.”
